q: ratio.c -- integer division bites
spec: A test run passed 7 of 9 checks. Keep both numbers in `int` variables
spec: and print exactly these four lines:
spec:
spec: `7 of 9 passed`
spec: `integer percent: 77`
spec: `real percent: 77.78`
spec: `majority: yes`
spec:
spec: The integer percent is 7 * 100 / 9 with whole-number division. The real
spec: percent is the same ratio as a `double`, shown with `%.2f`. Majority is
spec: a `bool`: more than half passed, printed as `yes` or `no`.
file: ratio.c
prog: #include <stdbool.h>
prog: #include <stdio.h>
prog: 
prog: int main(void)
prog: {
prog: 	int passed = 7;
prog: 	int total = 9;
prog: 	bool majority = passed * 2 > total;
prog: 
prog: 	printf("%d of %d passed\n", passed, total);
prog: 	printf("integer percent: %d\n", passed * 100 / total);
prog: 	printf("real percent: %.2f\n", (double)passed * 100 / total);
prog: 	printf("majority: %s\n", majority ? "yes" : "no");
prog: 	return 0;
prog: }
case: ratio
case: ratio | sed -n 2,3p
case: ratio; echo $?
hint: passed / total is 0 in integers -- multiply by 100 first, or cast one side to double
